1
00:00:00,133 --> 00:00:01,966
你有没有被一个章卡住过
Have you ever been held up by a stamp

2
00:00:02,200 --> 00:00:03,366
材料都带了
You brought all the documents

3
00:00:03,566 --> 00:00:04,533
字也签了
Signed your name

4
00:00:04,733 --> 00:00:05,666
人也到了
Showed up in person

5
00:00:05,833 --> 00:00:07,333
最后窗口的人说
Then the person at the counter says

6
00:00:07,700 --> 00:00:08,666
还差一个章
You're still missing one stamp

7
00:00:08,900 --> 00:00:10,600
你当时可能会很烦
You probably found that annoying

8
00:00:10,833 --> 00:00:11,666
心里想
Thinking

9
00:00:11,833 --> 00:00:14,233
不就是一块刻了字的东西吗
It's just a piece of stone with characters carved in it

10
00:00:14,433 --> 00:00:16,966
为什么它比我本人还管用
Why does it carry more weight than I do

11
00:00:17,166 --> 00:00:19,433
这就是印章最反直觉的地方
This is the most counterintuitive thing about stamps

12
00:00:19,566 --> 00:00:21,033
它看起来像形式
It seems like just a formality

13
00:00:21,200 --> 00:00:22,400
但很多时候
But a lot of times

14
00:00:22,766 --> 00:00:25,333
它比一句承诺更有分量
It carries more weight than a promise

15
00:00:25,500 --> 00:00:28,833
很多人以为印章代表的是规矩
Many people think a stamp represents rules

16
00:00:29,000 --> 00:00:30,866
我觉得不只如此
I think it's more than that

17
00:00:31,033 --> 00:00:36,566
印章真正代表的是一套把信任固定下来的办法
What a stamp really represents is a way to lock trust in place

18
00:00:36,766 --> 00:00:37,733
人会变
People change

19
00:00:37,966 --> 00:00:38,800
话会变
Words change

20
00:00:39,033 --> 00:00:40,066
记忆会变
Memories change

21
00:00:40,300 --> 00:00:42,333
但盖下去的那一下
But that moment a stamp goes down

22
00:00:42,566 --> 00:00:44,133
会把责任留在纸上
It pins responsibility to the paper

23
00:00:44,366 --> 00:00:46,366
这条视频不讲书法
This video isn't about calligraphy

24
00:00:46,633 --> 00:00:47,833
也不讲收藏
Or collecting

25
00:00:48,033 --> 00:00:49,566
只讲一个判断
Just one idea

26
00:00:49,733 --> 00:00:51,966
信用不是凭感觉相信一个人
Credit isn't about feeling like you trust someone

27
00:00:52,200 --> 00:00:57,200
信用是让承诺可以被看见被保存被追责
Credit is making promises visible storable and accountable

28
00:00:57,366 --> 00:00:58,600
你去办一件事
You go handle something

29
00:00:58,800 --> 00:00:59,866
对方说可以
The other person says sure

30
00:01:00,033 --> 00:01:01,466
你心里不一定踏实
You might not feel reassured

31
00:01:01,600 --> 00:01:03,033
对方写下来
They write it down

32
00:01:03,333 --> 00:01:04,533
你会踏实一点
You feel a bit better

33
00:01:04,700 --> 00:01:06,233
对方写完还盖了章
They stamp it after signing

34
00:01:06,500 --> 00:01:08,566
你才觉得这事终于有了着落
Only then do you feel it's finally settled

35
00:01:08,733 --> 00:01:09,600
这很有意思
That's pretty interesting

36
00:01:09,833 --> 00:01:11,266
明明说话的是人
The person doing the talking is human

37
00:01:11,566 --> 00:01:12,966
签字的也是人
The one signing is human too

38
00:01:13,100 --> 00:01:14,766
但真正让你放心的
But what actually puts you at ease

39
00:01:14,966 --> 00:01:16,666
偏偏是那个红色印记
Is that little red mark

40
00:01:16,833 --> 00:01:17,766
为什么
Why

41
00:01:17,900 --> 00:01:20,200
因为印章把一个人的口头意思
Because a stamp turns one person's spoken intent

42
00:01:20,366 --> 00:01:22,400
变成了一个组织的正式承认
Into an organization's official acknowledgment

43
00:01:22,566 --> 00:01:24,066
一个人嘴上答应你
Someone verbally agrees to something

44
00:01:24,233 --> 00:01:25,833
他可以说自己忘了
They can say they forgot

45
00:01:25,966 --> 00:01:27,600
他说那不是最终意见
They can say that wasn't their final word

46
00:01:27,800 --> 00:01:29,533
他说当时没理解清楚
They can say they didn't understand at the time

47
00:01:29,966 --> 00:01:30,933
可章一盖
But once that stamp goes down

48
00:01:31,133 --> 00:01:32,433
意思就不一样了
It means something different

49
00:01:32,600 --> 00:01:34,333
它像是在纸上说
It's like saying on paper

50
00:01:34,566 --> 00:01:35,633
这不是闲聊
This isn't small talk

51
00:01:35,833 --> 00:01:37,133
这不是客气
This isn't being polite

52
00:01:37,233 --> 00:01:38,433
这是要负责的
This means accountability

53
00:01:38,633 --> 00:01:40,566
你在公司里见过这种场景
You've seen this at work

54
00:01:40,700 --> 00:01:42,366
领导口头说没问题
Your boss says verbally no problem

55
00:01:42,700 --> 00:01:44,166
你还是会追一句
But you still follow up with

56
00:01:44,333 --> 00:01:45,966
那我发个邮件确认一下
Let me send an email to confirm

57
00:01:46,133 --> 00:01:47,966
客户饭桌上说合作愉快
A client says great working with you over dinner

58
00:01:48,166 --> 00:01:49,966
你还是会等合同盖章
But you still wait for the contract to be stamped

59
00:01:50,133 --> 00:01:51,833
朋友说下周一定还钱
A friend says they'll definitely pay you back next week

60
00:01:51,966 --> 00:01:53,166
你心里可能想
You might think

61
00:01:53,366 --> 00:01:54,933
最好有转账记录
Better have a transfer record

62
00:01:55,133 --> 00:01:56,400
这不是你冷漠
This isn't you being cold

63
00:01:56,600 --> 00:01:57,600
这是你知道
This is you knowing

64
00:01:57,933 --> 00:01:59,633
信任不能只靠气氛
Trust can't rely on vibes alone

65
00:01:59,966 --> 00:02:01,000
气氛会过去
Vibes fade

66
00:02:01,166 --> 00:02:02,266
证据会留下
Evidence stays

67
00:02:02,533 --> 00:02:04,666
印章的价值就在这里
That's the value of a stamp

68
00:02:04,766 --> 00:02:06,800
它把飘在空气里的承诺
It takes promises floating in the air

69
00:02:07,100 --> 00:02:08,866
压成一个可以保存的痕迹
And presses them into something you can keep

70
00:02:09,000 --> 00:02:10,566
人情可以让事情开始
Favors can get things started

71
00:02:10,733 --> 00:02:13,033
但凭证才能让事情落地
But only proof makes things real

72
00:02:13,166 --> 00:02:14,066
换到古代
Go back to ancient times

73
00:02:14,233 --> 00:02:15,966
一枚官印为什么重要
Why was an official seal so important

74
00:02:16,133 --> 00:02:17,400
不是因为它好看
Not because it looked nice

75
00:02:17,566 --> 00:02:19,333
而是因为它能告诉别人
But because it told people

76
00:02:19,533 --> 00:02:21,533
谁有资格发号施令
Who had the authority to give orders

77
00:02:21,733 --> 00:02:23,466
谁能代表官府收税
Who could collect taxes on behalf of the government

78
00:02:23,733 --> 00:02:25,266
谁能出具文书
Who could issue official documents

79
00:02:25,566 --> 00:02:27,633
谁做错事要承担后果
Who would be held accountable for mistakes

80
00:02:27,800 --> 00:02:28,966
如果没有印章
Without a seal

81
00:02:29,200 --> 00:02:31,200
一个陌生人拿着一张纸说
Some stranger walks up with a piece of paper saying

82
00:02:31,500 --> 00:02:33,133
我是官府派来的
I was sent by the government

83
00:02:33,300 --> 00:02:34,133
你信不信
Would you believe them

84
00:02:34,233 --> 00:02:35,066
很难信
Hard to believe

85
00:02:35,300 --> 00:02:36,966
因为你不知道他是谁
Because you don't know who they are

86
00:02:37,133 --> 00:02:39,533
也不知道他背后有没有真正的权力
Or whether they actually have real authority

87
00:02:39,700 --> 00:02:42,600
印章就像一个古代的身份验证
A seal was like ancient identity verification

88
00:02:42,766 --> 00:02:44,200
它让远处的权力
It let authority from far away

89
00:02:44,533 --> 00:02:46,166
能在一张纸上出现
Show up on a single piece of paper

90
00:02:46,366 --> 00:02:47,933
也让陌生人之间
And it let strangers

91
00:02:48,166 --> 00:02:50,966
不用每次从零开始互相证明
Skip having to prove themselves from scratch every time

92
00:02:51,166 --> 00:02:53,400
这就是社会运行里很关键的一点
This is a crucial part of how society works

93
00:02:53,566 --> 00:02:55,566
我们不可能认识每一个人
We can't possibly know everyone

94
00:02:55,766 --> 00:02:58,133
也不可能亲自核实每一句话
Or verify every single claim ourselves

95
00:02:58,333 --> 00:03:00,333
所以社会需要符号
So society needs symbols

96
00:03:00,633 --> 00:03:01,600
需要证件
Needs credentials

97
00:03:01,900 --> 00:03:02,766
需要章
Needs stamps

98
00:03:03,133 --> 00:03:05,566
需要一套大家都认的记号
Needs a set of marks everyone recognizes

99
00:03:05,733 --> 00:03:07,400
你去银行办业务
You go to the bank

100
00:03:07,633 --> 00:03:09,133
工作人员不认识你
The staff doesn't know you

101
00:03:09,233 --> 00:03:11,200
但他会看身份证
But they check your ID

102
00:03:11,366 --> 00:03:13,133
你在网上买东西
You shop online

103
00:03:13,500 --> 00:03:15,000
你不认识商家
You don't know the seller

104
00:03:15,233 --> 00:03:16,733
但你会看平台认证
But you check if they're platform verified

105
00:03:16,900 --> 00:03:19,066
你买一个不熟悉的品牌
You buy from an unfamiliar brand

106
00:03:19,300 --> 00:03:20,433
你不认识老板
You don't know the owner

107
00:03:20,633 --> 00:03:23,133
但你会看有没有授权质检和售后
But you check for authorized quality inspection and warranty

108
00:03:23,300 --> 00:03:25,433
这些东西其实都在做一件事
All these things are really doing one thing

109
00:03:25,633 --> 00:03:29,200
把不认识的人暂时变成可以交易的人
Turning strangers into people you can do business with

110
00:03:29,400 --> 00:03:30,833
不过这里也有危险
But there's danger here too

111
00:03:30,966 --> 00:03:35,000
很多骗局利用的正是我们对符号的信任
Many scams exploit exactly our trust in symbols

112
00:03:35,100 --> 00:03:37,066
一个看起来正规的公章
An official looking stamp

113
00:03:37,300 --> 00:03:39,033
一个看起来专业的证书
A professional looking certificate

114
00:03:39,233 --> 00:03:41,366
一个看起来很像官方的页面
An official looking website

115
00:03:41,500 --> 00:03:43,000
都会让人放松警惕
Can all make you let your guard down

116
00:03:43,166 --> 00:03:44,966
你以为自己相信的是人
You think you believe in the person

117
00:03:45,200 --> 00:03:47,166
其实你相信的是那套外壳
But you actually believe in the packaging

118
00:03:47,366 --> 00:03:49,433
所以印章不是让你盲目信
So a stamp isn't telling you to blindly trust

119
00:03:49,600 --> 00:03:51,366
印章是在提醒你
It's reminding you

120
00:03:51,533 --> 00:03:53,800
真正的信任必须能找到责任人
Real trust means being able to find who's responsible

121
00:03:54,000 --> 00:03:55,666
只看章不看谁负责
Looking only at the stamp without checking who's behind it

122
00:03:55,900 --> 00:03:58,633
就像只看包装不看里面装的是什么
Is like looking at the packaging without checking what's inside

123
00:03:58,700 --> 00:04:01,233
今天很多人已经很少摸到实体印章
Today most people rarely touch physical stamps

124
00:04:01,400 --> 00:04:02,966
但印章从来没有消失
But stamps never really disappeared

125
00:04:03,133 --> 00:04:04,633
它只是换了样子
They just changed form

126
00:04:04,766 --> 00:04:06,400
蓝色认证标识
Blue verification badges

127
00:04:06,600 --> 00:04:08,066
企业官方账号
Official business accounts

128
00:04:08,300 --> 00:04:09,333
平台担保
Platform guarantees

129
00:04:09,533 --> 00:04:10,566
电子签名
Electronic signatures

130
00:04:10,800 --> 00:04:12,000
品牌授权
Brand authorizations

131
00:04:12,233 --> 00:04:13,400
用户评价
User reviews

132
00:04:13,566 --> 00:04:15,966
这些都是现代社会的印章
These are all stamps of modern society

133
00:04:16,133 --> 00:04:17,666
你点外卖时
When you order food delivery

134
00:04:17,933 --> 00:04:19,433
会看店铺评分
You check the restaurant rating

135
00:04:19,633 --> 00:04:20,766
你买课程时
When you buy a course

136
00:04:20,966 --> 00:04:22,833
会看讲师背景
You check the instructor's background

137
00:04:22,966 --> 00:04:24,666
你投简历时
When you send a resume

138
00:04:24,966 --> 00:04:26,733
会写学校公司证书
You list your school company and certifications

139
00:04:26,900 --> 00:04:27,833
你去相亲
You go on a blind date

140
00:04:28,000 --> 00:04:30,800
对方也会问工作学历家庭
The other person asks about your job education and family

141
00:04:31,000 --> 00:04:32,400
听起来很现实
Sounds pretty pragmatic

142
00:04:32,533 --> 00:04:34,400
但这背后有一个简单原因
But there's a simple reason behind it

143
00:04:34,566 --> 00:04:36,566
陌生人之间的信任太贵了
Trust between strangers is expensive

144
00:04:36,700 --> 00:04:39,033
大家都需要一个能快速判断的标记
Everyone needs a quick way to judge

145
00:04:39,133 --> 00:04:41,233
你可能不喜欢被标签化
You might not like being labeled

146
00:04:41,400 --> 00:04:44,366
但你每天也在使用标签判断别人
But you use labels to judge others every day

147
00:04:44,533 --> 00:04:46,333
这就是印章的现代版本
That's the modern version of a stamp

148
00:04:46,533 --> 00:04:48,133
它不一定是红色的
It might not be red

149
00:04:48,300 --> 00:04:50,866
但它依然在帮人节省判断成本
But it still saves people the cost of judging

150
00:04:51,000 --> 00:04:52,233
一个好品牌
A good brand

151
00:04:52,400 --> 00:04:53,966
就是给产品盖章
Is a stamp on a product

152
00:04:54,166 --> 00:04:55,733
一个稳定的履历
A steady track record

153
00:04:55,933 --> 00:04:57,466
就是给个人盖章
Is a stamp on a person

154
00:04:57,733 --> 00:04:59,366
一个清楚的作品集
A clear portfolio

155
00:04:59,533 --> 00:05:00,933
就是给能力盖章
Is a stamp on ability

156
00:05:01,133 --> 00:05:02,600
一个靠谱的人设
A reliable reputation

157
00:05:02,800 --> 00:05:04,466
就是给陌生关系盖章
Is a stamp on an unfamiliar relationship

158
00:05:04,600 --> 00:05:05,466
你会发现
You'll notice

159
00:05:05,700 --> 00:05:07,366
普通人在社会里吃亏
Ordinary people lose out in society

160
00:05:07,566 --> 00:05:09,600
很多时候不是因为没有能力
Often not because they lack ability

161
00:05:09,733 --> 00:05:13,233
而是因为能力没有留下可被识别的印章
But because their ability hasn't left a recognizable stamp

162
00:05:13,433 --> 00:05:14,800
你说自己很负责
You say you're responsible

163
00:05:15,100 --> 00:05:16,633
别人听完就过去了
People hear it and move on

164
00:05:16,833 --> 00:05:18,600
但你每次准时交付
But every time you deliver on time

165
00:05:18,800 --> 00:05:20,566
每次把过程记录清楚
Every time you document the process clearly

166
00:05:20,766 --> 00:05:22,833
每次出问题主动补救
Every time you fix problems proactively

167
00:05:23,000 --> 00:05:24,466
这些痕迹堆起来
These traces pile up

168
00:05:24,633 --> 00:05:26,633
就会变成你的信用印章
And become your credit stamp

169
00:05:26,833 --> 00:05:29,033
信用不是靠一句我靠谱
Credit isn't built on saying I'm reliable

170
00:05:29,200 --> 00:05:32,533
信用是别人不用见你也能找到你靠谱的证据
Credit is others being able to find proof you're reliable without seeing you

171
00:05:32,733 --> 00:05:34,000
这句话听着有点冷
Sounds a bit cold

172
00:05:34,133 --> 00:05:35,733
但对普通人很重要
But it matters for ordinary people

173
00:05:35,800 --> 00:05:37,066
因为世界太大
Because the world is too big

174
00:05:37,300 --> 00:05:39,733
别人没有那么多时间慢慢了解你
People don't have enough time to get to know you slowly

175
00:05:39,900 --> 00:05:42,833
你要让自己的可信度有地方落下来
You need to give your credibility somewhere to land

176
00:05:43,000 --> 00:05:44,633
这件事放到职场里
Take this into the workplace

177
00:05:44,766 --> 00:05:45,766
就更明显
And it's even more obvious

178
00:05:45,933 --> 00:05:47,333
同样说我能做
Same words I can do it

179
00:05:47,566 --> 00:05:48,633
新人说出来
When a newcomer says it

180
00:05:48,766 --> 00:05:50,066
别人可能会犹豫
People might hesitate

181
00:05:50,200 --> 00:05:53,133
一个总能按时交付的人说出来
When someone who always delivers on time says it

182
00:05:53,300 --> 00:05:54,666
别人就会放心很多
People feel much more at ease

183
00:05:54,966 --> 00:05:55,866
为什么
Why

184
00:05:56,133 --> 00:05:57,666
因为他过去的记录
Because their past record

185
00:05:57,900 --> 00:05:59,866
已经替他盖过很多次章
Has already stamped for them many times

186
00:06:00,033 --> 00:06:02,266
你不需要每次都重新证明自己
You don't need to prove yourself from scratch every time

187
00:06:02,566 --> 00:06:04,533
是因为你之前留下的痕迹
Because the traces you left before

188
00:06:04,600 --> 00:06:05,933
还在替你说话
Are still speaking for you

189
00:06:06,233 --> 00:06:07,600
这就是信用的复利
This is the compound interest of credit

190
00:06:07,766 --> 00:06:09,533
它不会一夜之间出现
It doesn't appear overnight

191
00:06:09,700 --> 00:06:12,000
也不会靠一句漂亮话建立
And it isn't built on fancy words

192
00:06:12,133 --> 00:06:14,366
它是一次一次小事累出来的
It accumulates from small things one by one

193
00:06:14,533 --> 00:06:15,533
一次准时
Being on time once

194
00:06:15,733 --> 00:06:16,966
一次说到做到
Following through once

195
00:06:17,133 --> 00:06:18,866
一次把问题讲清楚
Explaining a problem clearly once

196
00:06:19,100 --> 00:06:20,866
一次不把责任推给别人
Not passing the blame once

197
00:06:21,033 --> 00:06:23,400
这些东西当时看起来很普通
These seem ordinary in the moment

198
00:06:23,566 --> 00:06:24,866
但过一段时间
But after a while

199
00:06:25,100 --> 00:06:27,200
它们会变成别人心里的印章
They turn into a stamp in other people's minds

200
00:06:27,333 --> 00:06:28,133
相反
On the flip side

201
00:06:28,233 --> 00:06:30,566
一个人如果总是口头热情
If someone is always enthusiastic with words

202
00:06:30,766 --> 00:06:31,800
行动含糊
Vague in action

203
00:06:32,000 --> 00:06:32,933
承诺很满
Making big promises

204
00:06:33,166 --> 00:06:34,233
交付很飘
But delivering nothing solid

205
00:06:34,433 --> 00:06:36,000
那他也会有一个印章
They'll have a stamp too

206
00:06:36,300 --> 00:06:37,966
只是那个章上写着
Except it says

207
00:06:38,166 --> 00:06:39,133
不太可靠
Not very reliable

208
00:06:39,300 --> 00:06:41,600
这也是为什么信用很贵
That's also why credit is expensive

209
00:06:41,800 --> 00:06:42,733
钱可以借
Money can be borrowed

210
00:06:42,933 --> 00:06:44,066
职位可以换
Jobs can be changed

211
00:06:44,300 --> 00:06:46,566
但一个人长期留下的印象
But the impression someone leaves over time

212
00:06:46,733 --> 00:06:48,666
很难靠一次解释洗掉
Is hard to wash away with one explanation

213
00:06:48,900 --> 00:06:50,566
所以印章这件事
So the whole stamp thing

214
00:06:50,800 --> 00:06:52,866
不只是权力机构的工具
Isn't just a tool for those in power

215
00:06:53,000 --> 00:06:54,933
它也是每个普通人的提醒
It's also a reminder for every ordinary person

216
00:06:55,033 --> 00:06:56,400
你每天怎么做事
How you handle things every day

217
00:06:56,566 --> 00:06:58,166
其实都在给自己刻章
Is actually carving your own stamp

218
00:06:58,300 --> 00:07:00,466
那普通人怎么用好这个判断
So how can ordinary people use this insight

219
00:07:00,600 --> 00:07:01,400
第一
First

220
00:07:01,566 --> 00:07:04,000
重要事情别只听口头承诺
Don't just rely on verbal promises for important things

221
00:07:04,166 --> 00:07:06,800
不是说人与人之间不能讲情分
Not saying you can't show goodwill between people

222
00:07:06,966 --> 00:07:08,333
而是越重要的事
But the more important something is

223
00:07:08,433 --> 00:07:10,200
越要留下清楚凭证
The more you need clear proof

224
00:07:10,433 --> 00:07:11,933
合作要有合同
Partnerships need contracts

225
00:07:12,100 --> 00:07:13,266
借钱要有记录
Loans need records

226
00:07:13,433 --> 00:07:15,166
工作安排要有确认
Work arrangements need confirmation

227
00:07:15,333 --> 00:07:17,633
售后承诺要有截图
After sales promises need screenshots

228
00:07:17,833 --> 00:07:19,433
你不是在防所有人
You're not guarding against everyone

229
00:07:19,566 --> 00:07:21,400
你是在保护未来的自己
You're protecting your future self

230
00:07:21,666 --> 00:07:22,466
第二
Second

231
00:07:22,733 --> 00:07:24,200
不要只看章
Don't just look at the stamp

232
00:07:24,400 --> 00:07:26,400
要看章后面能不能追责
Check whether you can actually hold someone accountable behind it

233
00:07:26,566 --> 00:07:28,066
一个证书很漂亮
A certificate looks great

234
00:07:28,200 --> 00:07:29,566
但发证的人是谁
But who issued it

235
00:07:29,733 --> 00:07:31,200
一个账号很官方
An account looks official

236
00:07:31,400 --> 00:07:33,400
但联系方式是否真实
But is the contact info real

237
00:07:33,566 --> 00:07:35,033
一份合同盖了章
A contract has a stamp

238
00:07:35,300 --> 00:07:37,200
但主体名称是否一致
But does the entity name match

239
00:07:37,366 --> 00:07:38,733
这些细节很烦
These details are tedious

240
00:07:38,966 --> 00:07:40,866
可它们就是信任的地基
But they're the foundation of trust

241
00:07:41,033 --> 00:07:42,000
很多人被骗
Many people get scammed

242
00:07:42,200 --> 00:07:43,333
不是因为太傻
Not because they're stupid

243
00:07:43,533 --> 00:07:45,366
而是因为太想快点放心
But because they want too badly to feel safe quickly

244
00:07:45,566 --> 00:07:47,066
骗子最会做的事
What scammers do best

245
00:07:47,233 --> 00:07:49,833
就是给你一个看起来很放心的符号
Is give you a symbol that looks trustworthy

246
00:07:50,100 --> 00:07:50,900
第三
Third

247
00:07:51,200 --> 00:07:53,533
给自己积累可见的信用
Build visible credit for yourself

248
00:07:53,700 --> 00:07:55,566
不要只说自己努力
Don't just say you work hard

249
00:07:55,733 --> 00:07:56,766
留下作品
Leave behind your work

250
00:07:56,900 --> 00:07:58,466
不要只说自己靠谱
Don't just say you're reliable

251
00:07:58,633 --> 00:07:59,566
留下记录
Leave behind a record

252
00:07:59,966 --> 00:08:01,266
不要只说自己专业
Don't just say you're professional

253
00:08:01,433 --> 00:08:02,466
留下案例
Leave behind case studies

254
00:08:02,566 --> 00:08:04,600
你每一次按时交付
Every time you deliver on time

255
00:08:04,766 --> 00:08:06,266
每一次清楚沟通
Every time you communicate clearly

256
00:08:06,500 --> 00:08:07,833
每一次出问题不躲
Every time you don't dodge when things go wrong

257
00:08:08,000 --> 00:08:09,333
都是在给自己盖章
You're stamping for yourself

258
00:08:09,500 --> 00:08:11,266
这件事尤其适合普通人
This especially matters for ordinary people

259
00:08:11,366 --> 00:08:14,466
因为普通人没有太多天生背书
Because ordinary people don't have much natural backing

260
00:08:14,700 --> 00:08:16,133
没有名校光环
No elite school prestige

261
00:08:16,333 --> 00:08:17,800
没有大公司职位
No big company title

262
00:08:18,000 --> 00:08:19,566
没有家里资源铺路
No family resources paving the way

263
00:08:19,766 --> 00:08:20,633
那怎么办
So what do you do

264
00:08:20,900 --> 00:08:23,266
就只能把每一次小交付
Turn every small delivery

265
00:08:23,566 --> 00:08:25,233
做成别人能看见的证据
Into evidence others can see

266
00:08:25,433 --> 00:08:27,033
你帮朋友做一件事
When you help a friend

267
00:08:27,233 --> 00:08:28,733
要把结果说清楚
Make the results clear

268
00:08:28,900 --> 00:08:30,166
你做一个项目
When you do a project

269
00:08:30,366 --> 00:08:31,966
要把过程沉淀下来
Document the process

270
00:08:32,100 --> 00:08:33,366
你学一个技能
When you learn a skill

271
00:08:33,533 --> 00:08:34,566
要留下作品
Leave something to show for it

272
00:08:34,700 --> 00:08:36,133
你答应一个时间
When you commit to a deadline

273
00:08:36,366 --> 00:08:38,633
就尽量别让别人催第二遍
Try not to make people chase you twice

274
00:08:38,800 --> 00:08:40,366
这些动作不华丽
These actions aren't flashy

275
00:08:40,533 --> 00:08:41,566
但很管用
But they work

276
00:08:41,633 --> 00:08:44,800
因为它们会慢慢减少别人对你的不确定
Because they gradually reduce others' uncertainty about you

277
00:08:45,033 --> 00:08:46,166
别人选择你
When others choose you

278
00:08:46,333 --> 00:08:48,333
不是因为你喊得最大声
It's not because you shout the loudest

279
00:08:48,533 --> 00:08:50,433
而是因为跟你合作时
But because when they work with you

280
00:08:50,600 --> 00:08:52,033
他不用一直担心
They don't have to constantly worry

281
00:08:52,200 --> 00:08:53,433
担心很贵
Worrying is expensive

282
00:08:53,700 --> 00:08:54,766
放心很值钱
Peace of mind is valuable

283
00:08:54,933 --> 00:08:56,333
一个靠谱的人
A reliable person

284
00:08:56,533 --> 00:08:58,366
其实是在替别人省心
Is actually saving others mental effort

285
00:08:58,600 --> 00:09:00,200
省下来的那部分心力
That saved mental energy

286
00:09:00,366 --> 00:09:02,400
就是他的信用溢价
Is their credit premium

287
00:09:02,600 --> 00:09:04,666
所以别总想着一次证明自己
So stop trying to prove yourself in one shot

288
00:09:04,966 --> 00:09:06,133
信用这件事
With credit

289
00:09:06,333 --> 00:09:07,633
最怕一次太满
The worst thing is overpromising once

290
00:09:07,766 --> 00:09:10,266
最靠得住的是长期不掉链子
The most reliable thing is not dropping the ball over the long term

291
00:09:10,400 --> 00:09:12,466
如果你不知道从哪里开始
If you don't know where to start

292
00:09:12,633 --> 00:09:14,366
就从三件小事开始
Start with three small things

293
00:09:14,566 --> 00:09:15,633
说清时间
Be clear about timing

294
00:09:15,800 --> 00:09:17,000
说清边界
Be clear about boundaries

295
00:09:17,200 --> 00:09:18,166
说清结果
Be clear about outcomes

296
00:09:18,333 --> 00:09:19,933
能周五交就别说周三
If you can finish by Friday don't promise Wednesday

297
00:09:20,133 --> 00:09:22,766
只能做到八分就别承诺十分
If you can only deliver eight don't promise ten

298
00:09:22,966 --> 00:09:25,400
出了问题先说明现在卡在哪里
When problems come up first explain where you're stuck

299
00:09:25,566 --> 00:09:27,333
这些话听起来不漂亮
These words aren't pretty

300
00:09:27,433 --> 00:09:28,966
但它会让别人知道
But they let others know

301
00:09:29,166 --> 00:09:30,833
你不是靠情绪做事
You don't act on emotion

302
00:09:31,000 --> 00:09:32,666
你是靠规则做事
You act on principles

303
00:09:32,833 --> 00:09:35,000
一个人一旦让别人觉得可预测
Once someone finds you predictable

304
00:09:35,200 --> 00:09:36,433
信用就开始出现
Credit starts to form

305
00:09:36,566 --> 00:09:38,066
因为可预测本身
Because being predictable itself

306
00:09:38,333 --> 00:09:40,200
就是一种高级的可靠
Is a high level of reliability

307
00:09:40,433 --> 00:09:41,800
一天一天盖下去
Stamp it day after day

308
00:09:41,966 --> 00:09:43,400
最后别人提到你
Eventually when someone mentions you

309
00:09:43,600 --> 00:09:45,666
心里会自动浮出一个章
A stamp automatically comes to mind

310
00:09:45,900 --> 00:09:47,233
这个人可以托付
This person can be trusted

311
00:09:47,433 --> 00:09:49,800
这比任何漂亮介绍都更有分量
That carries more weight than any fancy introduction

312
00:09:49,966 --> 00:09:52,933
长期可靠才是最好的个人名片
Long term reliability is the best personal brand

313
00:09:53,100 --> 00:09:54,433
这个章不一定红
This stamp might not be red

314
00:09:54,600 --> 00:09:56,933
但它会慢慢印在别人心里
But it slowly imprints in people's minds

315
00:09:57,100 --> 00:09:59,066
印章最值得我们学的
The most valuable lesson from stamps

316
00:09:59,300 --> 00:10:00,733
不是权力的威风
Isn't the power it commands

317
00:10:00,833 --> 00:10:02,333
而是责任的重量
But the weight of responsibility

318
00:10:02,500 --> 00:10:04,033
盖章的那一下很轻
That moment of stamping is light

319
00:10:04,233 --> 00:10:05,833
可它告诉所有人
But it tells everyone

320
00:10:06,000 --> 00:10:07,233
这句话有人认
Someone stands behind these words

321
00:10:07,433 --> 00:10:08,666
这件事有人管
Someone is accountable for this

322
00:10:08,933 --> 00:10:11,066
这个承诺不是风一吹就散
This promise won't blow away in the wind

323
00:10:11,300 --> 00:10:12,666
真正可靠的人
A truly reliable person

324
00:10:12,933 --> 00:10:14,400
不是从不说错话
Isn't someone who never says the wrong thing

325
00:10:14,600 --> 00:10:16,366
而是愿意让自己的承诺留下痕迹
But someone willing to let their promises leave a trace

326
00:10:16,600 --> 00:10:17,366
下一期我们聊陶渊明
Next time we'll talk about Tao Yuanming

327
00:10:17,366 --> 00:10:19,200
很多人以为他是在躺平
Many people think he was just slacking off

328
00:10:19,200 --> 00:10:21,400
但从生活经济学看
But from a life economics perspective

329
00:10:21,733 --> 00:10:25,233
他做的事可能更清醒
What he did might have been more clear headed

330
00:10:25,366 --> 00:10:26,833
他不是放弃生活
He didn't give up on life

331
00:10:26,900 --> 00:10:30,900
而是在主动降低人生的固定成本
He was actively reducing the fixed costs of living

332
00:10:30,900 --> 00:10:31,700
我们下期见
See you next time
